align   unattainable-through-text=yes: detokenizing the chain's 32 ids gives 205 bytes (valid UTF-8, 0 control-class tokens); `llama-tokenize -f` on those bytes returns 32 ids of which only 30 are equal, first divergence index 3 (chain 78392 vs 750). The byte string is forced by the ids (byte-level BPE is byte-preserving and token->piece is a bijection), so that candidate is the only candidate and no text prefill reproduces them. Reproduction: quantization/evidence/llama-stimulus-alignment-2026-10-27.md
align   attainable-through-raw-ids=yes: tools/llama_tokens_dump.cpp feeds the ids through batch.token[] with no tokenizer in the process image; run tools/llama_aligned_run.py run <tag>, then re-run this mode with --llama-manifest pointing at that run's manifest (the aligned fixture records its path). This manifest (checkpoints/llama-dump-manifest-2026-10-27-run-a.json) is the template-wrapped run-a, which is why the line above is NOT-ALIGNED and not a refusal to look.
align   consequence: mode numeric refuses; mode structural stands alone.

